## Can AI Create Passive Income?

Artificial intelligence does not create truly passive income. Software cuts the initial cost of producing ebooks, digital art, or background music, but sustained sales still depend on marketing, distribution, and ongoing upkeep.

Selling AI-created goods also introduces platform requirements and legal limits. [Amazon KDP](https://kdp.amazon.com/en_US/help/topic/G200672390) requires publishers to disclose AI-generated text, images, or translations when releasing a book. According to Etsy's seller policies, [Etsy](https://www.etsy.com/legal/creativity/) places prompt-generated items into its "designed by" tier, mandates disclosure in item listings, and forbids selling AI prompt bundles entirely. If you generate audio with [Suno](https://help.suno.com/en/articles/2416769), you receive commercial rights only while paying for a Pro or Premier subscription. Music created on Suno's free tier remains non-commercial, and the company keeps ownership of those tracks.

Intellectual property rights create another commercial hurdle. The U.S. Copyright Office issued guidance stating that purely AI-generated material is not registrable for copyright protection. Prompts alone do not provide sufficient human control, which means anyone can legally duplicate and sell an entirely machine-generated asset without infringing on your ownership.

Unrealistic promises around automated earnings have also triggered regulatory penalties. Federal Trade Commission enforcement actions target businesses that market automated storefronts as effortless investments. In February 2024, the FTC settled with the operators of Automators AI, who pitched passive investment income from AI-managed Amazon and Walmart storefronts. The resulting settlement banned those operators from e-commerce business opportunities and imposed an order topping $21 million. Later that year, the agency targeted Ascend Ecom over claims that AI tools would produce thousands in monthly passive revenue.

Treat artificial intelligence as a production tool rather than an automated income stream. If you want reliable earnings, explore the active, client-facing services detailed in our guide on [how to make money with AI](/guides/how-to-make-money-with-ai/).